From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RISE Project CI <ci@riseproject.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover bundled third-party licences

`license_files=["LICENSE.md"]` is an explicit PEP 639 list, so it replaces
setuptools' default `LICEN[CS]E*` glob rather than adding to it: a
`LICENSE.<dep>` dropped at the project root to cover a library
`auditwheel repair` vendors into the wheel (libdbus-1 and its transitive
closure) is silently ignored. Widening the list to also match `LICENSE.*`
picks those up with no other packaging change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not filed; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index a5ab373..179211b 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ skbuild.setup(
     long_description=long_description,
     long_description_content_type="text/markdown",
     license_expression="BUSL-1.1",
-    license_files=["LICENSE.md"],
+    license_files=["LICENSE.md", "LICENSE.*"],
     packages=["simplepyble"],
     package_dir={"": "simplepyble/src"},
     package_data={"simplepyble": ["py.typed", "*.pyi"]},
-- 
